---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Qingdao Transportation — Airport, Train & Getting Around" description="How to get to Qingdao and get around. Liuting Airport metro, high-speed trains, ferries, metro, buses, taxis, and Didi. Complete transit guide." pageType="Article">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="tag mb-3">Transport</p>
      <h1 class="mb-6">Getting to Qingdao & Getting Around</h1>
      <p class="body-lg mb-10 max-w-[65ch]">Qingdao is well-connected by air, rail, and sea. Once you arrive, the metro, Didi, and buses cover the city efficiently. This guide covers every option with real prices, times, and tips from repeated visits.</p>

      <!-- ═══════════ GETTING TO QINGDAO ═══════════ -->
      <h2 class="h3 mb-6">Getting to Qingdao</h2>

      <!-- Airport -->
      <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-4">
          <span class="text-3xl">✈️</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Qingdao Jiaodong International Airport (TAO)</h3>
            <p class="caption">30km north of the city center. Opened 2021, replacing the old Liuting Airport.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">To/From the City</h4>
            <div class="space-y-3 caption">
              <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="tag shrink-0 bg-green-100 text-green-800">Best</span><div><strong>Metro Line 8</strong> — 40 min to Qingdao North Station, then transfer to Line 1/2/3. ¥7. Runs 06:00–22:30. Trains every 8 min. English signage throughout.</div></div>
              <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="tag shrink-0 bg-blue-100 text-blue-800">Easy</span><div><strong>Didi (ride-hailing)</strong> — 45 min to Shinan District. ¥100–150 depending on traffic. Pay via Alipay, no cash needed. Use the Didi mini-app inside Alipay.</div></div>
              <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="tag shrink-0">Bus</span><div><strong>Airport shuttle</strong> — 60 min to city. ¥20. Runs to Qingdao Station area. Slower but cheapest after metro. Luggage space limited.</div></div>
              <div class="flex gap-2"><span class="tag shrink-0 bg-red-100 text-red-800">Avoid</span><div><strong>Street taxis at arrivals</strong> — Drivers approach you before the official queue. Charge 2–3x the meter rate. If you must take a taxi, go to the official queue and insist on the meter (¥10 flag fall).</div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">Airport Facilities</h4>
            <ul class="caption space-y-2">
              <li><strong>WiFi:</strong> Free, no phone verification needed. Connect before exiting.</li>
              <li><strong>SIM card:</strong> China Unicom kiosk after customs, before arrivals hall. ¥100 for 20GB/30 days + local number. Bring your passport.</li>
              <li><strong>Currency exchange:</strong> Counters near baggage claim. Rates are poor; exchange only a small amount.</li>
              <li><strong>Food:</strong> Limited options past security. Better to eat in the city.</li>
              <li><strong>Luggage storage:</strong> Available at the arrivals level. ¥10–20/bag/day.</li>
              <li><strong>English:</strong> Basic signage in English. Staff at the Unicom kiosk speak some English.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Train -->
      <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-4">
          <span class="text-3xl">🚆</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">High-Speed Train</h3>
            <p class="caption">Qingdao has two main stations. Both serve high-speed rail (G-trains and D-trains).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Route</th><th class="text-right py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Duration</th><th class="text-right py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Price (2nd class)</th><th class="text-right py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Frequency</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3">Beijing → Qingdao</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">3–3.5h</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥250–350</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">Every 30 min</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3">Shanghai → Qingdao</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">5–5.5h</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥300–400</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">Hourly</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3">Nanjing → Qingdao</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">3–3.5h</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥250–300</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">Every 1–2h</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3">Jinan → Qingdao</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">1.5–2h</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥120–170</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">Every 20 min</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3">Yantai → Qingdao</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">1.5h</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥80–110</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">Hourly</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">Which Station?</h4>
            <div class="caption space-y-2">
              <p><strong>Qingdao Station (青岛站)</strong> — Right in Old Town. Walk to Zhanqiao Pier in 10 min. Most convenient for tourists. Served by some G-trains and most D-trains.</p>
              <p><strong>Qingdao North Station (青岛北站)</strong> — In Licang District. Metro Line 1/2/3 connection. 25 min to Shinan by metro. More train options, especially from Beijing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">How to Book</h4>
            <div class="caption space-y-2">
              <p><strong>Trip.com</strong> — English interface, accepts foreign cards. Book up to 15 days ahead. Small service fee (~¥15).</p>
              <p><strong>12306.cn</strong> — Official China Railway site. Chinese only but cheapest. Requires Chinese ID or passport registration.</p>
              <p><strong>At the station</strong> — Bring your passport. Ticket windows accept cash and Alipay. Arrive 30+ min early for security check.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Ferry -->
      <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-10">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-4">
          <span class="text-3xl">⛴️</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Ferry</h3>
            <p class="caption">Qingdao Port connects to several domestic and international destinations.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">Domestic Ferries</h4>
            <div class="caption space-y-2">
              <p><strong>Dalian:</strong> Overnight ferry, 6–8 hours. Cabins from ¥200. Departs evening, arrives morning. Scenic Bohai Sea crossing.</p>
              <p><strong>Yantai:</strong> 2–3 hours. ¥80–150. Multiple daily departures. Fastest sea connection to Qingdao.</p>
              <p><strong>Weihai:</strong> 3 hours. ¥100–160. Less frequent, check schedule in advance.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">International Ferries</h4>
            <div class="caption space-y-2">
              <p><strong>Incheon (South Korea):</strong> 2–3 times per week. ~14 hours overnight. Cabins from ¥600–1,200. Check current schedule as routes change seasonally.</p>
              <p><strong>Shimonoseki (Japan):</strong> Service is suspended/resumed periodically. Check with Qingdao Port authority for latest status.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="caption mt-4"><strong>Tip:</strong> Qingdao Port Passenger Terminal is near the Old Town, about 20 min by taxi from Shinan. For the Dalian overnight ferry, book a 4-berth soft sleeper cabin for the best value.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- ═══════════ GETTING AROUND ═══════════ -->
      <h2 class="h3 mb-6">Getting Around Qingdao</h2>

      <!-- Metro -->
      <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-4">
          <span class="text-3xl">🚇</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Metro</h3>
            <p class="caption">7 lines covering the main city. Clean, efficient, and cheap.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Line</th><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Route</th><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Key Stations for Tourists</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Line 1</td><td class="py-2 px-3">North–South</td><td class="py-2 px-3 caption">Qingdao North Station, Qingdao Station</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Line 2</td><td class="py-2 px-3">East–West</td><td class="py-2 px-3 caption">May Fourth Square, Olympic Sailing Center</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Line 3</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Old Town loop</td><td class="py-2 px-3 caption">Zhanqiao (near), Badaguan, Shinan core</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Line 4</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Shibei connector</td><td class="py-2 px-3 caption">Beer Museum area</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Line 8</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Airport express</td><td class="py-2 px-3 caption">Airport → Qingdao North (40 min)</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Line 11</td><td class="py-2 px-3">East to Laoshan</td><td class="py-2 px-3 caption">Laoshan scenic area stops</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Line 13</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Huangdao/West</td><td class="py-2 px-3 caption">Golden Beach area</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="caption space-y-2">
          <p><strong>Fares:</strong> ¥2–7 depending on distance. Pay with Alipay transport code or buy single-journey tokens at machines (English available).</p>
          <p><strong>Hours:</strong> 06:00–22:30. Trains every 4–8 min during peak, 8–12 min off-peak.</p>
          <p><strong>Tips:</strong> Station signs are bilingual (Chinese + English). Download the Qingdao Metro app or use Alipay's transport QR code. Avoid Line 3 between 07:30–09:00 and 17:30–19:00 if possible.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Didi -->
      <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-4">
          <span class="text-3xl">🚗</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Didi (Ride-Hailing)</h3>
            <p class="caption">The best transport option for tourists. Chinese Uber, but easier.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">How to Use</h4>
            <ol class="caption space-y-1 list-decimal list-inside">
              <li>Open Alipay app → search "Didi" or tap the Didi mini-app icon</li>
              <li>Enter your destination (you can paste Chinese addresses)</li>
              <li>Choose ride type: Express (kuaiche) is cheapest, Premier (youxiang) is nicer</li>
              <li>Confirm. The driver will call if they cannot find you</li>
              <li>Payment is automatic via Alipay when you arrive</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">Prices & Tips</h4>
            <ul class="caption space-y-2">
              <li>Most city trips: ¥15–40</li>
              <li>Airport to Shinan: ¥100–150</li>
              <li>Cheaper than taxis, no negotiation needed</li>
              <li>No language barrier — the app shows the route</li>
              <li>Drivers rarely speak English; have your hotel address in Chinese</li>
              <li>Wait times: 2–5 min in Shinan, 5–10 min in outer areas</li>
              <li>Rush hour (07:30–09:00, 17:30–19:00): add 50% to fare, longer waits</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bus -->
      <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-4">
          <span class="text-3xl">🚌</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Bus</h3>
            <p class="caption">Extensive network covering the entire city. Cheap but challenging without Chinese.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="caption space-y-2">
          <p><strong>Fares:</strong> ¥1–2. Pay with Alipay transport code or exact change (no change given). Air-conditioned buses cost ¥2.</p>
          <p><strong>Useful routes for tourists:</strong></p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside ml-4 space-y-1">
            <li><strong>Bus 304:</strong> City center → Laoshan (Taiqing entrance). ~60 min. ¥2. The budget option for Laoshan.</li>
            <li><strong>Bus 26:</strong> Qingdao Station → Badaguan → May Fourth Square. Scenic coastal route.</li>
            <li><strong>Bus 316:</strong> Shinan District → Huangdao ferry terminal.</li>
            <li><strong>Bus 202:</strong> Old Town circular route, passing major attractions.</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Bus route numbers are displayed in Chinese at stops. Use Baidu Maps or Amap (高德地图) to plan bus routes. Google Maps does not work in China.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Taxi -->
      <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-4">
          <span class="text-3xl">🚕</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Taxi</h3>
            <p class="caption">Green taxis are common. Use Didi instead when possible.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="caption space-y-2">
          <p><strong>Fares:</strong> ¥10 flag fall (first 3km). ¥1.70/km after. Wait time ¥0.40/min. Airport surcharge ¥10.</p>
          <p><strong>Tips:</strong></p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside ml-4 space-y-1">
            <li>Always insist on the meter (打表, dǎ biǎo). If the driver refuses, get out.</li>
            <li>Airport taxis have a reputation for overcharging tourists. Use Didi.</li>
            <li>Have your destination written in Chinese to show the driver.</li>
            <li>Most drivers do not speak English. Some do not accept Alipay; carry cash.</li>
            <li>Receipts (发票, fā piào) are printed automatically. Keep them for expense claims.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Walking & Biking -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10">
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3 mb-3">
            <span class="text-2xl">🚶</span>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Walking</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="caption leading-relaxed">The Old Town (Shinan District) is very walkable. Zhanqiao Pier, the cathedral, Badaguan, and May Fourth Square are all within 30 minutes on foot. The seaside promenade runs 3km from May Fourth Square eastward — perfect for evening strolls.</p>
          <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Watch out for:</strong> Electric scooters on sidewalks. They are silent and fast. Always look both ways before crossing, even on pedestrian paths.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card p-6">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3 mb-3">
            <span class="text-2xl">🚲</span>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Bike / E-Scooter Rental</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="caption leading-relaxed">Shared bikes (Hello Bike, Meituan Bike) are available via Alipay scan. ¥1.50/30 min. Docked stations near May Fourth Square and major attractions. Dedicated bike lanes along the coast make cycling pleasant.</p>
          <p class="caption mt-2"><strong>Best ride:</strong> May Fourth Square → Olympic Sailing Center → Shilaoren Beach (20km coastal path). See the <a href="/qingdao-routes/cycling" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">cycling route guide</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick Comparison -->
      <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 mb-10">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-4">Transport Comparison</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Method</th><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Best For</th><th class="text-right py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Cost</th><th class="text-left py-2 px-3 font-semibold">Tourist-Friendly?</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Metro</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Airport, cross-city</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥2–7</td><td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="text-green-600 font-medium">★★★★★</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Didi</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Door-to-door, any trip</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥15–150</td><td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="text-green-600 font-medium">★★★★★</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Bus</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Budget, Laoshan (304)</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥1–2</td><td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="text-amber-600 font-medium">★★★☆☆</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Taxi</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Short trips, no app</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥10–60</td><td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="text-amber-600 font-medium">★★★☆☆</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Walking</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Old Town sightseeing</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">Free</td><td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="text-green-600 font-medium">★★★★★</span></td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"><td class="py-2 px-3 font-medium">Shared bike</td><td class="py-2 px-3">Coastal rides, short hops</td><td class="py-2 px-3 text-right">¥1.50/30min</td><td class="py-2 px-3"><span class="text-green-600 font-medium">★★★★☆</span></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Pro Tips -->
      <div class="card p-6 md:p-8 bg-[var(--color-accent-subtle)]/30">
        <h2 class="h3 mb-4">Local Transport Tips</h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 caption">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">Before You Arrive</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-1">
              <li>Download Alipay and set up payment</li>
              <li>Enable the Alipay transport QR code (for metro and buses)</li>
              <li>Bookmark your hotel address in Chinese characters</li>
              <li>Download Baidu Maps or Amap (Google Maps does not work)</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2">While You Are Here</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-1">
              <li>Metro is fastest during rush hour (roads are gridlocked)</li>
              <li>Didi is cheapest off-peak and for airport runs</li>
              <li>Old Town is best explored on foot — save the metro for long distances</li>
              <li>Bus 304 to Laoshan is cheap but slow; Didi is 40 min vs 60+ min by bus</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex gap-4">
        <a href="/qingdao-travel-guide" class="btn-outline">Travel Guide</a>
        <a href="/first-hour" class="btn-outline">First Hour Guide</a>
        <a href="/qingdao-itineraries/3-days" class="btn-ghost">3-Day Itinerary</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
